---
// Terms of Use. Plain-language, public-good terms for a free beta tool.
// NOTE: This is a starting template, not legal advice. Have it reviewed by a
// lawyer before relying on it, and fill in the governing-law state below.
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Eyebrow from "../components/Eyebrow.astro";

const updated = "September 22, 2026";

const h2 = "mt-10 text-2xl font-bold text-foreground";
const p = "mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground";
const ul = "mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground";
const a = "text-link underline underline-offset-2 hover:opacity-80";
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Use — VisaNav"
  description="The terms for using VisaNav, a free public-interest tool that helps immigrants find information and trustworthy help. VisaNav is not a law firm and does not provide legal advice."
  canonicalPath="/terms"
  translated={false}
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6">
    <Eyebrow items={["TERMS OF USE", "FREE PUBLIC TOOL"]} />

    <h1 class="mt-5 text-4xl font-bold text-foreground">Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <div class="vn-card mt-8 p-6">
      <p class="text-[13px] font-bold leading-5 text-foreground">
        VisaNav is not a law firm and does not provide legal advice.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-1.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        VisaNav gives general immigration information and points you to official
        sources and free or low-cost help. It is not a substitute for advice
        about your specific situation from a licensed attorney or a
        DOJ-accredited representative.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class={p}>
      These Terms of Use ("Terms") are an agreement between you and Victor
      Valdez, the individual who operates VisaNav ("VisaNav", "we", "us"). By
      using the VisaNav website and chat assistant (the "Service"), you agree to
      these Terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the Service.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>What VisaNav is</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      VisaNav is a free, public-interest tool, currently in beta. It answers
      immigration questions in plain language, links to official government
      sources, and lists nonprofit and pro-bono organizations that offer free or
      low-cost help. The information is general and may not fit your
      circumstances.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>No legal advice, no attorney-client relationship</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Nothing on the Service is legal advice, and using it does not create an
      attorney-client relationship with anyone. Immigration law is complex and
      changes often, and an answer that is right for one person can be wrong for
      another. Always confirm anything important with a qualified, accredited
      representative or attorney before you act on it. VisaNav is free: no one
      should ever ask you to pay to use it.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>The resource and representative directory</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      The Service lists organizations and representatives to help you find
      trustworthy assistance. We try to keep the directory accurate, but we do
      not employ, control, or guarantee any listed organization or person, and a
      listing is not an endorsement or a referral. Verify credentials yourself,
      including through the government's own rosters, before relying on anyone.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Accounts</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      You can use the chat assistant anonymously, without an account. If you
      choose to create an account, you are responsible for keeping your login
      details secure and for activity under your account. Provide accurate
      information and let us know if you believe your account has been
      compromised.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p class={p}>When using the Service, you agree not to:</p>
    <ul class={ul}>
      <li>Use it for any unlawful purpose or to harm others.</li>
      <li>
        Submit other people's personal information without their permission.
      </li>
      <li>
        Attempt to break, overload, scrape at scale, or gain unauthorized access
        to the Service or its data.
      </li>
      <li>
        Misrepresent the Service's output as legal advice from a licensed
        professional, or resell it as such.
      </li>
      <li>
        Interfere with security features, rate limits, or other users' access.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class={h2}>Availability and changes</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      The Service is offered on an "as is" and "as available" basis. Because it
      is a free beta run as a public good, we may change, suspend, or discontinue
      any part of it at any time, and we may update these Terms. When we make
      material changes to the Terms, we will update the date above. Continuing to
      use the Service after a change means you accept the updated Terms.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>No warranty</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      We work to keep the information accurate and current, but we do not warrant
      that it is complete, error-free, or up to date, or that the Service will be
      uninterrupted or secure. To the fullest extent permitted by law, we
      disclaim all warranties, express or implied.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, VisaNav and its operator will not
      be liable for any indirect, incidental, or consequential damages, or for
      any decisions you make based on the Service. The Service is a free
      information tool; it is not a legal representative and cannot be
      responsible for the outcome of your immigration matter.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Governing law</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of [Your U.S. state],
      United States, without regard to its conflict-of-laws rules, except where
      applicable law requires otherwise.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Contact</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Questions about these Terms? Email
      <a class={a} href="mailto:privacy@visanav.org">privacy@visanav.org</a>.
      See also our
      <a class={a} href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
